                <pb facs="0759" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.003/556: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-25T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 25, 1919,
                                noon.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 25,
                            9.85 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>My telegram of January 18, 1 p.m. The Chinese Government is very anxious to know
                    whether the American Government has agreed to the Shanghai tariff revision. I
                    sincerely hope that ratification has been effected as delay until meeting of
                    Congress would mean loss of many millions of dollars to the Chinese Government.
                    The Japanese Government has also made inquiry about this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
